cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LexEuropa in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "LexEuropa: citation-verified legal research over EU law"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Braun
    given-names: Florian
version: 0.9.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lumenworksco/-LexEuropa"
url: "https://lex.braunf.com/"
abstract: >-
  An open-model research assistant for EU law. Questions are answered in short statements, each tied to the
  exact article or judgment paragraph it comes from and checked by an existence gate and an independent judge
  model. The library holds 81 EU instruments (treaties, legislation, Court of Justice judgments) in English.
  It is a research aid and gives no legal advice.
keywords:
  - legal-tech
  - eu-law
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - citation-verification
  - lora
